WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.440
Good morning, John. Here in America, it is the day
after Thanksgiving, which means that it is Black Fri-

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.960
[TWITTER:] Hey, Hank! It’s Twitter...
It’s Twitter, I have a question.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:10.280
[HANK:] What?
[TWITTER:] What’s your most controversial opinion?

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.960
[HANK:] Oh come on, Twitter.
Why would I tell you that?

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.880
[TWITTER:] Content, man! It’s content!

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:20.200
It’s an easy format to put your own personal spin
on without having to come up with something fresh.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:26.220
[HANK:] Yeah… No, yeah, that makes sense, but look.
My most controversial opinions are pretty controversial.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:29.200
And they’re also like nuanced and take a
long time to explain.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:30.359
For example - 
[TWITTER:] No! God.

00:00:30.359 --> 00:00:34.010
You make everything so complicated.
You’re just supposed to something dumb

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:39.360
that everybody’s gonna be mad about, like,
“Indian food is bad and everyone knows it.”

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.860
[HANK:] Why would anyone say that?
Like even if I don’t like Indian food,

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:46.320
I recognize that some people must, right?
What’s the point?

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:49.460
[TWITTER:] To make people mad!
[HANK:] Yeah, you’re right…

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:53.740
[TWITTER:] It’s ENGAGING. I’m leading you
to the water here, but I can’t make you drink!

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:59.380
You just have to come up with something dumb
that 80 to 90% of people are gonna despise…

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:03.000
But then 10 to 20% of people will be on your
side and they will have your back,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.029
and that’s gonna keep the conversation going!

00:01:05.029 --> 00:01:08.180
[HANK:] Oh my God! Like... this seems complicated.

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:12.990
[TWITTER:] No one said any of this was easy,
baby! Your job is to make it look easy!

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:15.780
[HANK:] Well, actually… I think it is.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.340
[TWITTER:] What?
[HANK:] It’s easy.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.820
Butt is legs.
[TWITTER:] What?

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:21.780
[HANK:] Butt... is legs.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.680
[TWITTER:] That’s ludicrous… Butt is butt.

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:28.620
[HANK:] Butt is butt, but butt is also legs.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:29.940
[TWITTER:] Butt is butt.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:31.490
[HANK:] Butt is legs.

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:35.340
[TWITTER:] That’s… I mean,
the dumbest thing I’ve ever heard!

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:37.600
[HANK:] Look, your leg bone is in your butt.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:39.120
[TWITTER:] But you only have one butt!

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:42.560
[HANK:] I know! That’s what makes this such
an interesting sentence!

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:47.500
It’s grammatically confusing because you
have a singular butt, but plural legs!

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:50.760
But this isn’t a grammatical question,
it’s an anatomical one,

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:52.620
and BUTT. IS. LEGS!

00:01:52.639 --> 00:02:00.259
[TWITTER:] But scientifically, anatomically, your gut
is in your torso, and your gut ends in your butthole,

00:02:00.259 --> 00:02:02.919
which is your butt.
So butt is torso, right?

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:07.380
[HANK:] The butthole is not legs…
The butthole is not butt.

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:11.060
[TWITTER:] THE BUTTHOLE IS NOT BUTT?!!
It’s in the name!!

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:18.300
[HANK:] The butt transitions to butthole,
just as hand is not arm. Arm transitions into hand -

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:26.459
[TWITTER:] Okay, so hand is not arm! Then
shoulder is not arm. Then butt is not legs.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:27.960
[HANK:] Shoulder is arm.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:29.920
[TWITTER:] Don’t say it.
[HANK:] And butt is legs.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:36.640
[TWITTER:] AGGH!! GOD!! Okay, look… I can’t
tell you why, but you are obviously wrong.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:40.920
[HANK:]
YOU TOLD ME TO HAVE A CONTROVERSIAL OPINION!!!

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:43.640
WHY ARE YOU YELLING AT ME FOR HAVING ONE???

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:45.700
[TWITTER:]
Oh my God! I did, didn’t I??

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:50.380
Like, I had legitimate - I had forgotten!
Good - good work!

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:54.500
[HANK:] Twitter, this is the world that
we have chosen for ourselves!

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:57.520
[TWITTER:] You got any others?
[HANK:] Alright, second controversial opinion.

